install-info: make compare_entries_text a total order (cross-host determinism)

compare_entries_text() (the qsort comparator for Info `dir` menu entries) is
inconsistent: when two entries' names are equal case-insensitively AND the same
length, it returns `len1 <= len2 ? -1 : +1` == -1 for BOTH (a,b) and (b,a)
(e.g. "_Exit" vs "_exit", or the two same-name "WEOF:" entries in libc.info).
That violates qsort's antisymmetry requirement, so qsort()'s result is undefined
and differs between libc qsort implementations -> share/info/dir is byte-different
on macOS vs glibc build hosts, breaking a reproducible cross-built install.

Keep the existing "shorter (prefix) name first" rule for different-length names
(it is already consistent), and for equal-length case-insensitive ties break on
the full entry text (strcmp) so the comparator is a consistent total order and
qsort is well-defined and host-independent.  Faithful: only reorders, never drops.

--- a/install-info/install-info.c	2026-06-06 13:52:51
+++ b/install-info/install-info.c	2026-06-06 13:52:51
@@ -2832,8 +2832,20 @@
   else
     len2 = colon2 - text2;
   int result = mbsncasecmp (text1, text2, len1 <= len2 ? len1 : len2);
-  if (result == 0) /* Identical start, the longer goes last */
-    return len1 <= len2 ? -1 : +1;
+  if (result == 0)
+    {
+      /* One name is a case-insensitive prefix of the other: the shorter
+         (prefix) name sorts first, as upstream intended.  */
+      if (len1 != len2)
+        return len1 < len2 ? -1 : +1;
+      /* Names are equal case-insensitively AND the same length.  Break the tie
+         on the FULL entry text so the comparator is a consistent TOTAL order:
+         handles "_Exit" vs "_exit" (case only) and same-name/different-target
+         entries (e.g. two "WEOF:" lines).  The original always-(-1) here gave
+         cmp(a,b)==cmp(b,a)==-1 for such pairs -> inconsistent comparator ->
+         undefined qsort -> share/info/dir differs across build hosts.  */
+      return strcmp (text1, text2);
+    }
   else
     return result;
 }
